meta {
  name: 05-TakedownListing
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/api/admin/listings/{{targetListingId}}/takedown
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{jwt}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "reason": "Listing has been reported 3 times in 48h for off-platform-fee solicitation (the agent is asking applicants to pay 'inspection fee' via personal Opay before showing the unit). Confirmed via two reporter screenshots in support tickets #4413 and #4419. Taking down pending agent re-verification."
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  # This is the action that protects future Ngozis.

  Spec requires `reason` (minLength 0 again — same complaint as reject).
  Fine that the body schema accepts a long string. What I CAN'T do from
  the API:
  - Attach the reporter screenshots / ticket references as structured fields.
  - See, before I push this button, who reported this listing. I'm taking
    down on faith — the system gives me no way to cross-reference.
  - Notify the owner *with* the reason. The persona doc says owner gets a
    notification — but I have no way to verify what the owner actually
    sees. (And I shouldn't have to trust the implementation; I want a
    `notification_preview` in the takedown response.)

  Response per spec is empty (no body shown). I would expect the
  takedown to echo back at minimum: { listingId, status:'TAKEN_DOWN',
  takenDownAt, takedownReason } so I can paste that into the support
  ticket as proof of action.
}
